\newlabel{fig:heads}{{1}{5}{Distribution of head $\reff /n$ at 20\% of training and at the end, over all seeds. Dashed and dotted lines mark the claimed limits of 0.1 and 0.6. Heads do not form two groups on either side of these limits; the only heads above 0.6 are in pretrained \bert }{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces $\mathrm  {rank}_{\mathrm  {eff}}/n$ over training on a log scale. Thick lines show first, middle, and last layers (seed means), and the band shows the range over all heads and seeds. Rank rises under default initialization (top row). Later layers lose rank from a peaked start (bottom left) and in pretrained \textsc  {BERT}\xspace  , while first layers keep their initial level. Without label signal (bottom right), the last layer dips and then recovers.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rank}{{2}{5}{$\reff /n$ over training on a log scale. Thick lines show first, middle, and last layers (seed means), and the band shows the range over all heads and seeds. Rank rises under default initialization (top row). Later layers lose rank from a peaked start (bottom left) and in pretrained \bert , while first layers keep their initial level. Without label signal (bottom right), the last layer dips and then recovers}{figure.2}{}}
